<!--
  Declared breaks against 1.0.0-beta.1.1, permitted by the repository's prerelease-stability policy
  and required by it to be declared. One change accounts for both entries here: a Standing Order and
  a Referral rule return a verdict rather than a bare requirement — so an order held back by one of
  the three checks degrades to reviewer confirmation on the record instead of vanishing, and so a
  policy can name this write's review window — and both regain the conversation identity the
  specification declares an approval policy is given, supplied so a policy can BIND (a member-bound
  Standing Order), never so it can authorize the actor, which the framework does itself.

  Three entries left this file when the baseline moved from 1.0.0-beta.1 to 1.0.0-beta.1.1: the
  removal of the framework's stock risk formula, the risk threshold's type and the risk calculator's
  return type were breaks against beta.1 and are what beta.1.1 shipped, so against that baseline
  there is nothing left to declare.

  See CHANGELOG.md's upgrade notes.
-->
<Suppressions xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <Suppression>
    <DiagnosticId>CP0002</DiagnosticId>
    <Target>M:Affiant.Policies.Referrals.ReferralRuleBase.EvaluateAsync(Affiant.Abstractions.Models.Affidavit,System.Threading.CancellationToken)</Target>
    <Left>lib/net10.0/Affiant.Policies.dll</Left>
    <Right>lib/net10.0/Affiant.Policies.dll</Right>
    <IsBaselineSuppression>true</IsBaselineSuppression>
  </Suppression>
  <Suppression>
